{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773184456,"nonce":"E5BDThG6L5mp8jEkYQNgpGDttz4=","title":"auth-request.sh: auto-generated commit message has no markdown formatting, renders as unseparated blob","message":"When --commit-message is not supplied, auth-request.sh generates the message via:\n\n  git log --format=\"%s\" \"${base_branch}..${branch}\" | head -20\n\nThis yields newline-separated subject lines, but renderMarkdown() in the UI (standard markdown parser) collapses single newlines into inline text. Result: multi-commit branches appear as one continuous string with no visual separation.\n\nFix: use --format=\"- %s\" so each subject becomes a markdown list item.","files":null}]}